From c559287b51a4073d1bff1b248bed5c4ebfec98dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): denied-card self-check reads the
 screen's verdict, skips the history read for kept cards; document
 portable_wake_probes

Follow-ups to PR #1950 (review 5887663683, card t_01a1d3d6ec456452):

1. `denied_target` read only `latest_verdict` (hub_admission events) while the claim screen gates the self-check
   on `pickup.verdict` (that event, else the `created` payload's audit). It now reads `pickup.verdict`, so a card
   whose only verdict sits in its created payload is re-placed too. In practice `record_created` mirrors the
   creation audit as a hub_admission event: on the hub (read-only, 11-13) all 136 creation-time denies have the
   event and 0 cards carry a created-payload verdict without one, so this is a consistency fallback.
2. `kanban.placement.portable_wake_probes` is documented in user-guide/configuration.md. The docs-drift ratchet
   missed it because it only scanned `self.raw.get(...)` in kanban_placement.py; it now also scans `cfg.get(...)`
   in kanban_hub_admission_claim.py, which reads the placement section directly.
3. Per tick the self-check ran `ready_since` (all events + runs) before `keep_reason` for every judged card still
   on the hub. Keep reasons (regexes + one LIMIT 1 wake_check read) now run first. Measured for a dir-workspace
   card: denied_target 0.305 -> 0.017 ms at 50 events, 10.6 -> 0.016 ms at 2000 events.

Tests: test_kanban_claim_deny_selfcheck.py +3 (created-payload-only verdict repins; dir/host_repo kept cards
never call ready_since), test_docs_drift.py open-section key. Red before the fix: those 3 + the drift ratchet.
